  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid BISPHOSPHONATES Oral Formulation Version 1; Last updated 3/28/2013; Approved 4/19/2013. effective_date retains 2021-03-15 from the archived stub.",
    "Class pack: Actonel (all strengths), Atelvia, Binosto Eff, Boniva/ibandronate, and Fosamax + D. The step coverage text specifies ibandronate (generic Boniva). Preferred coverage for alendronate sodium 5/10/35/40/70 mg requires no step.",
    "Actonel, Atelvia, ibandronate and Fosamax + D require a completed ≥30-day alendronate trial or documented adverse reaction. If trial is not an option, medical rationale AND a letter of medical necessity are the alternate step pathway. Binosto additionally requires documentation supporting effervescent over tablet formulation, including when using the exception.",
    "Authorization (notes only): coverage may be approved for 1 year; manual review.",
    "Dispensing limit (notes only): 30-day supply of medication; manual review.",
    "Reminder: report negative side effects of prescription drugs to the FDA MedWatch program."
  ],
